# wordpos builds its index into wordnet-db's directory, not its own.
#
# pnpm's side-effects cache records that a package's build script has run and
# skips it next time, keyed on that package's own output. wordpos writes
# somewhere else entirely, so the cache says "built" while the four
# fast-index.*.json files are missing — and since 1.0 the fast index cannot be
# turned off, every lookup throws, and every card fails.
#
# It reproduces exactly where it matters: a clean `pnpm install
# --frozen-lockfile`, which is what CI and the Render blueprint both run. Found
# by installing into an empty worktree and asking for a word.
#
# The cost is that install scripts re-run on every install. In this workspace
# that is wordpos alone, and the whole install still takes about four seconds.
side-effects-cache=false
